              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 12,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "WYKhS",
                  "name": "One rasteriser, two ",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 3,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "TSym0",
                      "name": "T",
                      "fill": "$accent",
                      "content": "One rasteriser, two consumers",
                      "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                      "fontSize": 12,
                      "fontWeight": "700"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "IjPGz",
                      "name": "D",
                      "fill": "$ink-secondary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "The silhouette and the UV map are the same code with a different projection: points in, a dot grid out, then a braille or block encoding. Building it once is why these two panels cost less together than either would alone.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.55,
                      "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                      "fontSize": 11,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "p8MAMr",
                  "name": "Legibility is the op",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 3,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "M0Da1",
                      "name": "T",
                      "fill": "$accent",
                      "content": "Legibility is the open risk",
                      "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                      "fontSize": 12,
                      "fontWeight": "700"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "iXROg",
                      "name": "D",
                      "fill": "$ink-secondary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "A dense mesh projected naively fills every dot and reads as a rectangle. The mitigation is depth sorting with density falloff, and the fallback is that the panel still communicates bounds and proportion even when the form does not resolve. This is the one thing in the design that only rendering can settle.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.55,
                      "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                      "fontSize": 11,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "QnpZa",
                  "name": "Overlap is drawn, no",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 3,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "BmNaj",
                      "name": "T",
                      "fill": "$accent",
                      "content": "Overlap is drawn, not just counted",
                      "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                      "fontSize": 12,
                      "fontWeight": "700"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "wIIaw",
                      "name": "D",
                      "fill": "$ink-secondary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "UV shells that overlap paint in the error hue, so the panel shows where the problem is rather than only that it exists. That is the difference between a number and a diagnosis.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.55,
                      "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                      "fontSize": 11,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
