                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "TfmLB",
                  "name": "Notes",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 11,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "n7Lrt",
                      "name": "Why a prefix and not",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "layout": "vertical",
                      "gap": 3,
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "utOn7",
                          "name": "T",
                          "fill": "$accent",
                          "content": "Why a prefix and not always-live keys",
                          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                          "fontSize": 12,
                          "fontWeight": "700"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "cQEJW",
                          "name": "D",
                          "fill": "$ink-secondary",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "Sort, filter, export and the nine addresses already claim most of the single-letter namespace. Making split and close always-live would either collide with those or push them onto modifiers, and an accidental layout change costs more than one extra keystroke.",
                          "lineHeight": 1.55,
                          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                          "fontSize": 11,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "HNeZC",
                      "name": "Case-insensitive, wi",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "layout": "vertical",
                      "gap": 3,
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "h7Zm7o",
                          "name": "T",
                          "fill": "$accent",
                          "content": "Case-insensitive, with one exception",
                          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                          "fontSize": 12,
                          "fontWeight": "700"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "fpStQ",
                          "name": "D",
                          "fill": "$ink-secondary",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "Every single-letter binding accepts both cases and the footer shows the lowercase form. The g and G pair is the documented exception, because the vim convention for first and last is older and stronger than the rule.",
                          "lineHeight": 1.55,
                          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                          "fontSize": 11,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "FWg1k",
                      "name": "Mouse is additive, n",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "layout": "vertical",
                      "gap": 3,
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "quhjK",
                          "name": "T",
                          "fill": "$accent",
                          "content": "Mouse is additive, never required",
                          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                          "fontSize": 12,
                          "fontWeight": "700"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "FOsek",
                          "name": "D",
                          "fill": "$ink-secondary",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "Drag a divider to resize, click a panel to focus, click a border menu word to invoke it. Every one of those has a keyboard path in the table above, so a terminal that reports no mouse loses nothing.",
                          "lineHeight": 1.55,
                          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                          "fontSize": 11,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "Qqjvf",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 12955,
      "name": "PROPOSED 09 / Overlays",
      "clip": true,
      "width": 1240,
      "height": 880,
      "fill": "$surface-canvas",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 18,
      "padding": 28,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "VTojI",
          "name": "Heading",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "hnWik",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$ink-strong",
              "content": "PROPOSED 09  Overlays",
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 22,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "y4EOO3",
              "name": "Sub",
              "fill": "$ink-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Four overlays and no more. Each uses the double border reserved for elevation, dims the grid behind it, and closes on esc. The filter is deliberately not one of them: it lives in the panel border, because filtering is about one panel and an overlay would say otherwise.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "oVUy2",
          "name": "Row 1",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "gap": 26,
